# Test: redistribute-block-does-not-gate-peer-routes -- a `redistribute` block
#       does not touch the routes a peer announces.
#
# VALIDATES: spec-fixit-redistribution-chain-drops-silently. The peer announces
# 10.0.0.0/24 and `show bgp rib received` names it, while a `redistribute` block
# is configured that mentions neither BGP nor this peer.
#
# THE REDISTRIBUTE BLOCK IS THE VARIABLE. Its twin,
# redistribute-no-block-peer-route-reaches-rib.ci, is byte-identical except that
# it carries no `redistribute` block. Read the two together: the pair is what
# discriminates, because a daemon that delivers in neither config is broken
# somewhere else and a daemon that delivers in both has the property under test.
#
# The block imports `connected` into `fakedest`. It names no BGP source, so it
# derives no Loc-RIB binding and has nothing whatever to do with the prefix this
# test reads back. Its only job is to make configredist.Global() non-nil, which
# is the single condition the defect turned on.
#
# PREVENTS: the class the `bgp-redistribute` ingress filter belonged to
# (internal/component/bgp/plugins/redistribute_ingress, retired 2026-09-04). It
# was registered as an ingress POLICY filter and ended
# `return ev.Accept(route, ""), nil`. Every rule the config loader builds carries
# the enclosing `destination` key, and ImportRule.Accept rejects a rule whose
# Destination does not match the importing protocol, so an empty importing
# protocol was rejected by every production rule. The route was then dropped at
# notifyMessageReceiver, before caching and before delivery. One `redistribute`
# block anywhere in the config discarded EVERY route EVERY peer announced.
#
# That blast radius is what nobody was testing. The filter's own unit tests were
# green because they built ImportRule values with an empty Destination, which no
# config produces, and every other redistribution test asked whether a
# REDISTRIBUTED route arrived. This test asks the opposite question: what happens
# to a route redistribution was never asked about.
#
# The plumbing here is WRITTEN BY HAND on purpose. The peer carries an explicit
# `attach process bgp-rib` block and the config declares the plugin, so nothing
# in this scenario rests on the binding the redistribute block derives. A red
# here is about the ingress path and about nothing else.
#
# Three surviving guards cover the same class at three levels, and each one
# would go red on its own:
#   - TestNoIngressFilterGatesAPeerRouteOnRedistributionConfig runs every
#     registered ingress filter over a real UPDATE at the composition root
#   - TestImportRuleAcceptRefusesAnUnnamedImportingProtocol makes the empty
#     importing protocol a panic rather than a silent rejection
#   - this pair proves the daemon end to end, through the entry point an
#     operator uses

# ze-peer expectations
stdin=peer:terminator=EOF_PEER
option=tcp_connections:value=1
option=timeout:value=25s
# Hold the session open: a closed peer is a session-down event, which releases
# the peer RIB the observer is reading.
option=linger:value=true
option=asn:value=65001
# The route under test. It enters ze from the peer, which is the only scope the
# Adj-RIB-In fills from.
option=update:value=send-route:prefix=10.0.0.0/24:next-hop=10.0.0.1
# EOR from ze, so the peer has a deterministic message to wait on.
expect=bgp:conn=1:seq=1:hex=FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF00170200000000
EOF_PEER

# ze configuration
stdin=ze-bgp:terminator=EOF_CONF
plugin {
	external redist-blast-radius-test {
		run "ze-test fixture plugin/redistribute-block-does-not-gate-peer-routes"
		encoder json
	}
	internal bgp-rib {
		use bgp-rib
	}
}

# THE VARIABLE. Present here, absent in the twin, and identical in every other
# respect. `connected` into `fakedest` names neither BGP nor this peer.
redistribute {
	destination fakedest {
		import connected;
	}
}

bgp {
	peer peer1 {
		connection {
			remote {
				ip 127.0.0.1
			}
			local {
				ip 127.0.0.1
				accept false
			}
		}
		session {
			asn {
				local 65000
				remote 65001
			}
			router-id 10.0.0.1
			family {
				ipv4/unicast { prefix { maximum 10000; } }
			}
			capability {
				graceful-restart disable
			}
		}
		behavior {
			group-updates disable
		}

		attach process bgp-rib {
			receive [ update state refresh ]
			send [ update ]
		}
	}
}
EOF_CONF

# Process orchestration
cmd=background:seq=1:exec=ze-peer --port $PORT:stdin=peer
cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=ze -:stdin=ze-bgp:timeout=25s
expect=exit:code=0
